    description: "INV-hokin premise audit item 2, filed as its own row (2026-10-03). The live cron (.woodpecker/full-suite.yml test-all-packages) runs ONE pytest over packages/*/tests/ with --cov on every package's src and --cov-fail-under=100. The GHA full-suite it replaced ran each package's tests ALONE against that package's src. Under the union a line covered only by ANOTHER package's tests counts toward 100%, so AGENTS.md's \"tests must live in the same package as the code they cover (CI tests packages in isolation)\" is enforced by no live CI; per-PR woodpecker.yml and nightly.yml use the same union. Only local scripts/check-package-coverage checks isolation. It has bitten before (WI-tubuv: core 99% in isolation; WI-dojuh: cli.py uncovered in core isolation).\n\nThe full-suite header claimed \"a 100% union <=> every package at 100%\" as equivalent to the GHA per-package jobs; INV-hokin's branch corrected that comment and tests/test_full_suite_coverage_teeth.py now states the gap. WI-kahar's description says \"the whole-package ISOLATION run is event: cron only\" -- the cron run is NOT an isolation run; noted on WI-kahar.\n\nFIX SHAPE (not designed or measured here): a cron step that runs scripts/check-package-coverage (or the per-package loop) instead of, or beside, the union run. Cost NOT MEASURED in CI; WI-kahar measured pkgcov at 780 s wall on 6 cores locally."  # 605d
    fields: {}  # 605d
